description: Rules for PHP/Laravel code (controllers, models, services, routes, tests).
globs: ["app/**/*.php", "routes/**/*.php", "database/**/*.php", "tests/**/*.php"]
alwaysApply: true

# Architecture
- Controllers stay thin: validate request, delegate to services/use-cases, return response.
- Business logic lives in Services/Domain, not in controllers or views.
- Use Dependency Injection; limit facades in domain logic.
- Use Policies/Gates/Middleware for authz; do not sprinkle auth checks ad hoc.

# Database & Eloquent
- Use Eloquent/Query Builder with parameter binding; avoid raw SQL.
- No string-concatenated SQL with user input.
- Avoid SELECT *; select explicit columns.
- Consider indexes for frequently filtered/joined columns.
- Avoid N+1 queries; eager load relations when needed.

# Migrations/Seeders
- Always provide `up()` and `down()` for migrations.
- Seeders only for dev/test; do not ship production-only dummy data.

# Testing
- Add/maintain unit/feature tests for new/changed logic.
- Regression tests for reported bugs.

# File Size & Style
- Keep files under ~300 lines; split large classes.
- Follow PSR-12; consistent naming (StudlyCase classes, camelCase methods).
